    </li>
    <li>
      We may change our prices. We'll email your admins at least 30 days before a price increase applies to your Plan,
      and you can cancel before then.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a payment fails, Emploist keeps working for a short grace period. If the payment still hasn't gone through by
      then, your company becomes read-only until it's paid.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Free trial</h3>
  <p>
    Your company's first Plan can start with a free trial. You add a payment method at checkout, and Dodo charges for the
    first billing period when the trial ends, unless an admin cancels before then. Each company and each person may use
    only one free trial.
  </p>

  <h3>AI credits</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Ranking an application uses one Credit, and ranking it again uses another.</li>
    <li>
      Your Plan includes Credits for each billing period, as shown on our <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> when that
      period starts. They don't carry over to the next period.
    </li>
    <li>Admins can buy extra Credits in packs. Pack Credits don't expire, but they're lost if your company is deleted.</li>
    <li>
      Credits can only be bought and used while your Plan is active. They have no cash value, can't be transferred, and
      aren't refundable, except where the law requires. If a credit pack is refunded, its unused Credits are removed.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cancellation and refunds</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      An admin can cancel at any time from the Billing page. Your Plan stays active until the end of the current trial or
      billing period, and you won't be charged again.
    </li>
    <li>
      Payments are non-refundable. There are no refunds or credits for partial billing periods or unused Credits, except
      where the law requires one, for any proration credit shown at checkout when you switch to yearly billing, or if
      we stop offering Emploist (<a
        href="#suspension-and-termination">section 14</a
      >). Refunds are paid by Dodo.
    </li>
    <li>Deleting your company cancels your Plan immediately, without a refund, and permanently deletes its data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When your Plan isn't active</h3>
  <p>
    When your Plan ends, and before your company starts one, your company is read-only. Your team can still sign in, view
    its data, and export applications, but can't make most changes, applications aren't ranked, and your careers page
    stops taking applications.
  </p>

