    purposes and are bound by confidentiality duties, or as the other directs. This doesn't apply to information that is
    or becomes public through no fault of the recipient, that the recipient already had or developed independently, or
    that it received lawfully from someone else. Either of us may disclose Confidential Information when the law
    requires it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data-processing">13. Data processing</h2>
  <p>
    This section is our data processing agreement. It applies when we process personal data in Customer Data on your
    behalf. "Data protection laws" means the data protection and privacy laws that apply to Customer Data. Words such as
    "controller", "processor", "personal data", and "personal data breach" have the meanings given in the EU and UK
    General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), or the closest equivalents in other data protection laws.
  </p>

  <h3>Roles</h3>
  <p>
    You're the controller of personal data in Customer Data, and we're your processor. If you're a processor yourself,
    for example a recruiter hiring for a client, we're your subprocessor, and you confirm that your controller has
    authorized our processing. We're a controller for the personal data we use to run our business, such as your team
    members' account details, as our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> describes.
  </p>

  <h3>Details of the processing</h3>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Subject matter and duration</th>
        <td>Providing Emploist to you, for as long as you use it and until the Customer Data is deleted.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Nature and purpose</th>
        <td>
          Hosting, storing, displaying, and transmitting Customer Data, continuously, to provide Emploist: publishing
          careers pages, collecting applications, ranking them with AI while AI ranking is on, sending emails to
          applicants, sending data to the AI assistants your team members connect, supporting and securing Emploist, and
          creating aggregated or de-identified information to operate and improve Emploist (see section 7).
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Data subjects</th>
        <td>
