          referees in a resume.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Personal data</th>
        <td>
          Applicants' names, email addresses, phone numbers if you ask for them, resumes and everything in them, answers
          to your questions, match scores, hiring stages, emails sent to them, and your team's comments about them.
          Names and email addresses of team members and invitees as they appear in Customer Data. Any other personal
          data in your content.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Sensitive data</th>
        <td>
          Emploist doesn't ask for it, but resumes and answers may contain it. It's protected by the security measures
          below, and access is limited to your team and the AI assistants they connect, and to us and our subprocessors
          as needed to provide Emploist.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Locations and subprocessors</th>
        <td>
          As shown in our <a href="/privacy/#subprocessors">list of subprocessors</a>. We access Customer Data from
          India.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Our commitments</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Instructions.</strong> We process Customer Data only on your documented instructions, including about
      transfers to other countries, unless the law requires otherwise. In that case, we'll tell you first, unless the law
      forbids it. Your instructions are these Terms and how you and your team use and set up Emploist. When a team member
